@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Decreto-Lei 4.657/1942 (LINDB): the rules of the text that bear on time.
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT GOVERNS, and so what is computed here:
--   art. 1 caput    a law begins to bind forty-five days after its official publication, unless it says otherwise
--   art. 1 par. 1   abroad, three months after official publication, where Brazilian law is admitted there
--   art. 1 par. 3   a corrective republication before the law binds restarts that term
--   art. 1 par. 4   a correction to a text already in force counts as a new law
--   art. 7 par. 6   one year from the date of a foreign judgment (used by the conflict-of-laws module)
--   art. 19 sole    ninety days "counted from" a publication date
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT DOES NOT GOVERN, so each is a named REFUSE and never a default:
--   how a period "counted from" a day is counted (is the starting day itself counted?),
--   weeks, days of rest, holidays and recess, deemed service, the moment of the day a law binds,
--   subordinate legislation, and any definition of day, week, month or year.
--
-- Days of rest, holidays and recess are an INPUT (a LIST OF DATE the caller supplies); no calendar is written here.
-- This module imports only prelude and daydate. Its readings of "N days after" and "N months after" are forks F1 and F3
-- of NOTES.md; the readings it declines to choose are F2.

§ `LINDB: the time rules`

§§ `What the text does not answer`

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph, the one provision that says "counted from" (no provision says whether the starting day counts)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say whether the starting day counts` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"

@ref LINDB (no provision on weeks; the text never uses the unit)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text never speaks of weeks` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text never speaks of weeks, so no provision counts a period of weeks"

@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 1 and art. 7 par. 6, the provisions that count in months and years
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day` MEANS
    REFUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"

@ref LINDB (no provision on days of rest, holidays or recess)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text has no rule for a last day that falls on a day of rest` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"

@ref LINDB (no provision on service or notice)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text has no rule on deemed service` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text has no rule on when a document is treated as served"

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (the text gives a day and no moment of that day)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text gives no moment of the day` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 1 gives the day on which a law begins to bind and does not say from what moment of that day"

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (the text speaks of a lei and has no rule for subordinate legislation)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text has no rule for subordinate legislation` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 1 speaks of a lei and the text has no rule on when subordinate legislation comes into force"

@ref LINDB (no provision defines a time word)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text defines no time word` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not define day, week, month or year"

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput, a period is a whole number of units
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a period is a whole number of units` MEANS
    REFUSE "a period counted after a day is a whole number of units, none of them negative"

§§ `Art. 1 caput and par. 1: the point N units after a day`

-- src:10 | Art. 1o Salvo disposição contrária, a lei começa a vigorar em todo o país quarenta e cinco dias depois de oficialmente publicada.
-- src:11 | § 1o Nos Estados estrangeiros, a obrigatoriedade da lei brasileira, quando admitida, se inicia três meses depois de oficialmente publicada.
-- src:13 | § 2o (Revogado pela Lei nº 12.036, de 2009).
-- src:14 | § 3o Se, antes de entrar a lei em vigor, ocorrer nova publicação de seu texto, destinada a correção, o prazo deste artigo e dos parágrafos anteriores começará a correr da nova publicação.
-- src:15 | § 4o As correções a texto de lei já em vigor consideram-se lei nova.
@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10-15)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term in days before a law binds throughout Brazil` MEANS 45

@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 1 (src:11)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term in months before Brazilian law binds in a foreign State that admits it` MEANS 3

-- The day that is N days after D is D plus N: D itself is not counted (fork F1 of NOTES.md).
-- The text says "quarenta e cinco dias depois de oficialmente publicada" and gives no other rule for the word.
@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS
    IF n AT LEAST 0 AND n EQUALS FLOOR n
    THEN d PLUS n
    ELSE `a period is a whole number of units`

-- The day that is N months after D has D's day number, N calendar months on (fork F3).
-- Where the month reached is too short to have that number there is no such day, and the text does not say what to do:
-- 31 January plus one month, or 29 February plus one year, is refused and never clamped to the end of the month.
@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 1 (src:11)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `months after` d MEANS
    IF n AT LEAST 0 AND n EQUALS FLOOR n
    THEN IF DATE_DAY d AT MOST `Days in month` `the month reached` `the year reached`
         THEN YMD `the year reached` `the month reached` (DATE_DAY d)
         ELSE `the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day`
    ELSE `a period is a whole number of units`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR d TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year reached` MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month reached` MEANS (`the month count` MODULO 12) PLUS 1

§§ `Art. 1: the day a law begins to bind`

DECLARE `What an enactment says about its own commencement` IS ONE OF
    `nothing about when it comes into force`
    `a day on which it comes into force` HAS `the day it fixes` IS A DATE
    `that the day is to be fixed later` HAS `the day fixed so far` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Where the law is to bind` IS ONE OF
    `throughout Brazil`
    `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law`
    `in a foreign State that does not admit the binding force of Brazilian law`

-- The term of art. 1, counted from a start day: forty-five days in Brazil, three months in a foreign State that admits the law.
-- Where the law is not admitted abroad the text starts no binding force, so it gives no day.
@ref LINDB art. 1 caput, par. 1 (src:10-11)
GIVEN place IS A `Where the law is to bind`
      start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the term of art. 1 ends for` place `counting from` start MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `throughout Brazil` THEN
        `the day` `the term in days before a law binds throughout Brazil` `days after` start
    WHEN `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` THEN
        `the day` `the term in months before Brazilian law binds in a foreign State that admits it` `months after` start
    WHEN `in a foreign State that does not admit the binding force of Brazilian law` THEN
        `the text gives no day where Brazilian law is not admitted`

@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 1 (src:11)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text gives no day where Brazilian law is not admitted` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 1 par. 1 starts the binding force of Brazilian law abroad only where it is admitted, and gives no day where it is not"

-- Art. 1 par. 3: a new publication of the text, made to correct it, before the law binds, restarts the term from the new publication.
-- Art. 1 par. 4: a correction to a text already in force counts as a new law, so it never moves this law's day.
-- The corrections are taken in date order. A correction on the very day the law is to begin binding is refused:
-- it is "before" under par. 3 or "already in force" under par. 4 according to the moment of that day, and the text gives none.
@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 3, par. 4 (src:14-15)
GIVEN place IS A `Where the law is to bind`
      start IS A DATE
      corrections IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day art. 1 and its corrections fix for` place `counting from` start `with corrections` corrections MEANS
    CONSIDER corrections
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the end of the term from` start
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY later THEN
        IF c LESS THAN start
        THEN `a correction cannot precede the publication it corrects`
        ELSE IF c LESS THAN `the end of the term from` start
             THEN `the day art. 1 and its corrections fix for` place `counting from` c `with corrections` later
             ELSE IF c EQUALS `the end of the term from` start
                  THEN `a correction on the day the law is to begin binding`
                  ELSE `the end of the term from` start
    WHERE
        `the end of the term from` s MEANS `the day the term of art. 1 ends for` place `counting from` s

@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 3 (src:14)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a correction cannot precede the publication it corrects` MEANS
    REFUSE "a corrective republication cannot precede the publication it corrects"

@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 3, par. 4 (src:14-15)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a correction on the day the law is to begin binding` MEANS
    REFUSE "a corrective republication on the day the law is to begin binding comes before it binds under art. 1 par. 3 or after it binds under art. 1 par. 4, and the text gives no moment of that day"

-- Art. 1 par. 4 on its own: a correction published after the law binds is a new law; one published before is par. 3's.
@ref LINDB art. 1 par. 4 (src:15)
GIVEN correction IS A DATE
      `the day the law begins to bind` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a correction counts as a new law` correction `when the law binds on` `the day the law begins to bind` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF correction LESS THAN `the day the law begins to bind` THEN FALSE
        IF correction GREATER THAN `the day the law begins to bind` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `a correction on the day the law is to begin binding`

-- The day an enactment begins to bind.
-- "Salvo disposicao contraria" (art. 1 caput): the enactment's own provision on its commencement displaces the forty-five days.
-- The text does not say whether that provision may also displace the three months abroad, nor whether it may name a day before
-- the official publication; both are refused. A correction under par. 3 moves only the term of art. 1, not a day the enactment fixed.
@ref LINDB art. 1 caput, par. 1, par. 3, par. 4 (src:10-15)
GIVEN provision IS A `What an enactment says about its own commencement`
      place IS A `Where the law is to bind`
      published IS A DATE
      corrections IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day an enactment begins to bind` provision place published corrections MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `nothing about when it comes into force` THEN
        `the day art. 1 and its corrections fix for` place `counting from` published `with corrections` `the corrections in date order`
    WHEN `a day on which it comes into force` d THEN
        `the day an enactment fixes for itself` d place published
    WHEN `that the day is to be fixed later` fixed THEN
        CONSIDER fixed
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the enactment leaves its commencement day to be fixed later and none has been fixed`
        WHEN JUST d THEN `the day an enactment fixes for itself` d place published
    WHERE
        `the corrections in date order` MEANS map `to a date` (sort (map `to a day number` corrections))
        `to a day number` c MEANS Day c
        `to a date` n MEANS Date n

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput, "salvo disposicao contraria" (src:10)
GIVEN fixed IS A DATE
      place IS A `Where the law is to bind`
      published IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day an enactment fixes for itself` fixed place published MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `throughout Brazil` THEN
        IF fixed LESS THAN published
        THEN `the text does not say whether a contrary provision may fix a day before publication`
        ELSE fixed
    WHEN `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` THEN
        `the text does not say whether an own commencement provision displaces the term abroad`
    WHEN `in a foreign State that does not admit the binding force of Brazilian law` THEN
        `the text gives no day where Brazilian law is not admitted`

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say whether a contrary provision may fix a day before publication` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 1 caput lets a contrary provision displace the forty-five days and does not say whether it may fix a day before the official publication"

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput, par. 1 (src:10-11)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say whether an own commencement provision displaces the term abroad` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 1 caput allows a contrary provision and par. 1 does not, so the text does not say whether an enactment's own commencement provision displaces the three months abroad"

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput, "salvo disposicao contraria" (src:10)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the enactment leaves its commencement day to be fixed later and none has been fixed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the enactment leaves its commencement day to be fixed later and no day has been fixed"

-- The moment of the commencement day from which a law binds, as a second of the day.
@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10)
GIVEN `the commencement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the second of the commencement day from which a law binds` `the commencement day` MEANS
    `the text gives no moment of the day`

-- Whether a law that begins to bind on a given day binds at some moment of another day, or throughout it.
@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      c IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law binds at some moment of` d `when it begins to bind on` c MEANS
    d AT LEAST c

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      c IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law binds throughout` d `when it begins to bind on` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d LESS THAN c THEN FALSE
        IF d GREATER THAN c THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `the text gives no moment of the day`

@ref LINDB art. 1 caput (src:10)
GIVEN `the day it was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day subordinate legislation comes into force` `the day it was made` MEANS
    `the text has no rule for subordinate legislation`

§§ `Art. 7 par. 6: the point N years after a day`

-- src:33 | § 6⟦STRUCK: º⟧ O divórcio realizado no estrangeiro, se um ou ambos os cônjuges forem brasileiros, só será reconhecido no Brasil depois de 1 (um) ano da data da sentença, salvo se houver sido antecedida de separação judicial por igual prazo, caso em que a homologação produzirá efeito imediato, obedecidas as condições estabelecidas para a eficácia das sentenças estrangeiras no país. O Superior Tribunal de Justiça, na forma de seu regimento interno, poderá reexaminar, a requerimento do interessado, decisões já proferidas em pedidos de homologação de sentenças estrangeiras de divórcio de brasileiros, a fim de que passem a produzir todos os efeitos legais.
@ref LINDB art. 7 par. 6, "1 (um) ano da data da sentenca" (src:33)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `years after` d MEANS
    IF n AT LEAST 0 AND n EQUALS FLOOR n
    THEN `the day` (n TIMES 12) `months after` d
    ELSE `a period is a whole number of units`

§§ `Art. 19 sole paragraph: a period counted from a day`

-- src:67 | Parágrafo único. No caso em que a celebração dêsses atos tiver sido recusada pelas autoridades consulares, com fundamento no artigo 18 do mesmo Decreto-lei, ao interessado é facultado renovar o pedido dentro em 90 (noventa) dias contados da data da publicação desta lei.
@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph, "contados da data da publicacao" (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `days counted from` d MEANS
    `the text does not say whether the starting day counts`

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `months counted from` d MEANS
    `the text does not say whether the starting day counts`

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `years counted from` d MEANS
    `the text does not say whether the starting day counts`

@ref LINDB (the text never uses weeks)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `weeks counted from` d MEANS
    `the text never speaks of weeks`

-- The two readings of the starting day, each as a function that says which it is.
-- They are NOT defaults: the refusals above are the text's answer, and these answer a different question,
-- "if the starting day is not counted" or "if it is counted as the first day".
@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is not counted` n d MEANS
    `the day` n `days after` d

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is the first day` n d MEANS
    (`the day` n `days after` d) MINUS 1

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of N months counted from, if the starting day is not counted` n d MEANS
    `the day` n `months after` d

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of N months counted from, if the starting day is the first day` n d MEANS
    (`the day` n `months after` d) MINUS 1

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is not counted` n d MEANS
    `the day` n `years after` d

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is the first day` n d MEANS
    (`the day` n `years after` d) MINUS 1

@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph (src:67)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a period counted from a day has at least one whole day` MEANS
    REFUSE "a period counted from a day is a whole number of days, at least one"

-- Whether a day falls inside a period of N days counted from a start, answered only where both readings agree.
-- If the starting day is not counted the period is the days start+1 to start+N; if it is counted, start to start+N-1.
-- Before the start and after start+N both readings say outside; start+1 to start+N-1 both say inside;
-- the starting day and start+N are inside on one reading and outside on the other, so they are refused.
@ref LINDB art. 19 sole paragraph, "dentro em 90 (noventa) dias contados da data" (src:67)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      start IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` d `falls inside a period of` n `days counted from` start MEANS
    IF n AT LEAST 1 AND n EQUALS FLOOR n
    THEN BRANCH
             IF d LESS THAN start THEN FALSE
             IF d GREATER THAN start PLUS n THEN FALSE
             IF d EQUALS start OR d EQUALS (start PLUS n) THEN `the text does not say whether the starting day counts`
             OTHERWISE TRUE
    ELSE `a period counted from a day has at least one whole day`

§§ `Days of rest, holidays and recess: an input, and no rule in the text`

-- The rest days are supplied by the caller. The function reads them: a last day that is not one of them is its own last day;
-- one that is one of them is refused, because the text has no rule that carries it to another day.
-- Two or more rest days in a row at the end of a period make no difference: the first of them is already refused.
@ref LINDB (no provision on days of rest, holidays or recess)
GIVEN `the days of rest` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `the days of rest` `the last day` MEANS
    IF elem `the last day` `the days of rest`
    THEN `the text has no rule for a last day that falls on a day of rest`
    ELSE `the last day`

§§ `Deemed service`

@ref LINDB (no provision on service or notice)
GIVEN `the day it was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a document is treated as served` `the day it was sent` MEANS
    `the text has no rule on deemed service`

§§ `The meaning of time words`

DECLARE `Word for a length of time` IS ONE OF
    `the word day`
    `the word week`
    `the word month`
    `the word year`

-- The text defines none of them. What the point functions above take (a day is the unit of PLUS, a month is a calendar month,
-- a year is twelve of them) is the ordinary meaning of the word, recorded as fork F3, and is not something the text says.
@ref LINDB (no provision defines a time word)
GIVEN word IS A `Word for a length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days the text says is in` word MEANS
    `the text defines no time word`
